  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shri. Shrinivas P. Shetty vs Shri. Gururaj Ramachandra Basur on 26 February, 2013 Author: B S Indrakala Bench: B S Indrakala -1- In The High Court Of Karnataka Circuit Bench At Dharwad Dated This The 26Th Day Of February 2013 Present The Hon'Ble Mr.Justice H.Billappa And The Hon'Ble Mrs.Justice B.S.Indrakala Writ Appeal No.30890/2012 (Gm-Res) Between: 1. Shri.Shirnivas P.Shetty, Age: 45 Years, Occ: Business, R/O Shri Chaitanya General Stores, Saidapur, P.B.Road, Dharwad. 2. Managing Director, Shri Akshay Traders, No.8, Rajendra Prasad Colony, Hubli-580023. Rep. By Keshav Mahabaleshwar Hegde, R/O No.8, Rajendra Prasad Colony, Hubli-580023. ...Appellants (By Sri.B.D.Hegde & Sri.S.B.Patil, Advs.) And : 1. Shri Gururaj Ramachandra Basur, Age: Major, Occ: Food Inspector, H.D.M.C., Dharwad. -2- Shri. Shrinivas P. Shetty vs Shri. Gururaj Ramachandra Basur on 26 February, 2013 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/45709956/ 1 2. Hubli Dharwad Municipal Corporation, Reptd. By Its Commissioner, Hubli. 3. State Of Karnataka, Rep.By Chief Secretary, Bangalore. ...Respondents (By Sri.G.T.Gachchinamath, Adv.For R1 & R2, Sri.Mahesh Wodeyar, Aga For R3) This Appeal Is Field Under Section 4 Of The Karnataka High Court Act, Praying To [LEAKAGE_MASK] The Order Of Learned Single Judge Dated 03.07.2012 Passed In W.P.No.64280/2012 And The Writ Petition Be Allowed By Allowing This Writ Appeal. This Appeal Coming On For Orders This Day,",
    "facts": "Under Section 97 of the FSS Act, 2006, the proceedings are saved. 3. Aggrieved by that, the appellants have filed this appeal. 4. Briefly stated, the facts are: The first respondent visited the shop of the first appellant on 29.01.2011 and collected samples of coriander. Thereafter, a private complaint has been lodged on 11.07.2011 by the first respondent against the appellants. Cognizance has been taken and summons having been issued to the appellants. The appellants have appeared before the trial Court on 16.05.2012. Thereafter, the appellants have approached this Court in W.P.No.64280/2012 seeking to quash the proceedings in C.C.No.991/2011. The complaint has been lodged on 11.07.2011. Therefore, the proceedings are saved under Section 97 of the FSS Act, 2006. Sections 94 to 98 of FSS Act, 2006 have come into force with effect from July 2010. As on the date of complaint, i.e., 11.07.2011, the provisions of PFA Act, 1954 was in force.",
    "arguments": "5. The learned counsel for the appellants contended that Sections 94 to 98 of the FSS Act, 2006 have come into force with effect from July 2010 and therefore, the provisions of PFA Act, 1954 stood repealed and therefore, the proceedings are vitiated in law and the learned Single Judge was not justified in dismissing the writ petition.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "5. The learned counsel for the appellants contended that Sections 94 to 98 of the FSS Act, 2006 have come into force with effect from July 2010 and therefore, the provisions of PFA Act, 1954 stood repealed and therefore, the proceedings are vitiated in law and the learned Single Judge was not justified in dismissing the writ petition.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
